From 906da12f51cbd53bf8bc13df196281983f3fe5de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:58:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] soc: apple: add guarded probe-time AOP state snapshot

Add an independent default-off state_probe parameter for the controlled
iOS power-off to DFU experiment. Reuse the existing five-domain PMGR
guard before reading only CPU status at +0xb88 and outbox control at
+0x4020. CPU status is the raw +0xb88 word, so do not read it twice.

Log PMGR target/actual, raw status and the two bit-zero values on one
line, and expose the same frozen string in root-only state_probe debugfs.
Report unpowered only for a successfully observed zero AOP ACTUAL;
mark wrapper fields skipped on any guard refusal. Preserve unknown for
transitions and errors rather than inventing a halted or powered state.
Defer until PMGR providers exist without reading the wrapper.

State-only mode requires no debug or ring parameter and maps only the
two required wrapper resources. It can coexist with ring diagnostics,
blocks the active driver before resource access, and never writes,
resumes a domain, touches a FIFO or sends a mailbox message.

Signed-off-by: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
